From 521af82fb168e65883782bd4602791db3e478a6e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 10:48:42 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] v2.8.7: the diag stops lying, and every page can reach the
 manual

Four changes, no C. Nothing here can wedge a router, which is the point of
shipping it on a stable base.

THE DIAG (v1.3.7 -> v1.3.8). Two counter defects, both of which made the diag
misreport a state rather than fail - the worst way for a triage tool to be
wrong, because the output looks healthy and authoritative either way.

Section 10 piped `tmctl getqcfg` through `head -3`, keeping qid/priority/qsize
and cutting weight/minBufs/schedMode/shaper plus the ret-code line. Those three
survivors are programmed by setqcfg unconditionally while every rate element
sits behind its own guard, so a box whose class rates never landed printed a
per-queue block byte-identical to a healthy one. Section 10 could not tell
"shaping" from "armed but toothless". Now one line per queue carrying every
field - and SHORTER than the form it replaces, 7 lines against 21 - plus a
[TMCTL-ERR] tag when ret code is non-zero, which the truncation used to discard.
The same block had already been rewritten once, for a truncation-shaped
misdiagnosis; that fix split the engines and left the truncation on the type-11
side, the branch with seven shapers to verify instead of one.

Section 19b counted syslog LINES, not events. hostapd repeats the same
disassociated line for one flap, commonly twice and in bursts of up to ten
inside a single second. Measured over a 48 h span on metal: 2810 lines against
411 unique (timestamp, MAC) events, 6.8x inflation; the top station read
1057 (~21/h) when the truth was 218 (~4.5/h). Both the 19b table and the
section 0b finding were fed from the raw count and now dedup on
(timestamp, MAC, event). The finding threshold (200) is deliberately unchanged:
against deduped events it stops firing on ordinary roaming while a real loop
still trips it. An inflated churn figure makes an already-benign device look
like a router fault.

THE MANUAL. Twelve pages gained a "?" in their heading linking to their section
of REAPER-GUIDE.md - QoS, QoS Diagnostics, Traffic, Devices, Connections,
Wireless, WiFi Pro, Diagnostics, Firmware, Analytics, Policy Routing, AI
Advisor. Five already had one, so every Reaper page now reaches the guide. It
reuses the existing RABT_43 key, so there are no new i18n keys and no
translation pass owed; the dict lockstep is untouched by that change. The guide
itself was pushed first, deliberately, so all 15 anchors resolve on the first
boot that carries them rather than 404-ing until a later push.

I18N. RFW_257 ("Other") minted and TRANSLATED in all 25 packs, and the IPv6
protocol select's BOTH label switched to the already-translated RFW_252 - the
last RFW_ residual. TCP and UDP stay literal; they are protocol names. The
value="TCP|UDP|BOTH|OTHER" attributes are untouched and still uppercase, because
rc/firewall.c does an exact case-sensitive strcmp on them and a translated value
would break the rule format in 24 languages. Adaptive_Others was deliberately
not reused: it is plural and names an Adaptive QoS category, which is the same
class of mistake as reusing ASUS's option_both_direction for "Both".

DEAD CODE. Reaper_Wireless.asp's scan pin carried a comment claiming
pinTarget() substitutes the 80 MHz block containing the winner, and a ternary
appending "<- <original>" when the pin differed from the scanned best. The
substitution was removed deliberately - it is exactly what made "best" and
"applied" disagree in the field - so pinTarget() returns its argument and that
condition can never be true. Comment corrected, dead ternary removed, function
kept. No behaviour change.

Dict lockstep 6745 -> 6746 (RFW_257 only). Diag verified by extracting its awk
programs and running them against fixtures; the guard lives in the lean repo at
build-scripts/ci/check_diag_counters.sh and is wired into patch-apply-check, so
it now asserts against the reconstructed series rather than a local tree.
---
 release/src-rt/version.conf | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/release/src-rt/version.conf b/release/src-rt/version.conf
index ddd2915acc..284cb10e6b 100644
--- a/release/src-rt/version.conf
+++ b/release/src-rt/version.conf
@@ -4,6 +4,6 @@ KERNEL_VER_AM=$(subst .,,$(KERNEL_VER))
 FS_VER_AM=$(subst .,,$(FS_VER))
 
 SERIALNO=102.8
-EXTENDNO=Reaper_v2.8.6
+EXTENDNO=Reaper_v2.8.7
 
 RCNO=0
